  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies a noise-optimized variational quantum classifier (NO-VQC) for predicting BET index movement against 9 other market indices, using 3 qubits for the main financial experiments, 8 qubits in gradient studies, and illustrative synthetic circuits up to 13 qubits. It reports that NO-VQC can improve over the baseline VQC and sometimes reduce overfitting, but classical methods such as logistic regression and SVM remain competitive, with median test accuracies around 0.71 in the best reported classical settings.",
